,"issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- v4.6.2.stable.mono.official [71f334935] (Linux)\n- v4.7.beta2.mono.official [777579205] (Linux)\n- v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935] (Linux)\n- v4.7.beta2.official [777579205] (Linux)\n\n- v4.6.2 Windows \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable.mono - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sat, 09 May 2026 11:29:28 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.24 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen connecting a Steam Controller (2026) to my PC and setting the Desktop Configuration to act as a regular gamepad, godot will not recognize any input. Other applications do receive input, for example [Gamepad Tester](https://hardwaretester.com/gamepad), the KDE Game Controller tester in the settings or the Godot Engine Web Editor.\n\nThe gamepad does however work if I add Godot to Steam and launch it from there.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Connect a Steam Controller (2026)\n- Open Steam and set the Desktop Configuration to the Gamepad template\n- Open Godot\n- Open the MRP\n- Start the game\n- Try to move the charater using the joystick\n  - On the Steam Controller (2026), nothing will happen\n  - On a different controller, the godot icon will move\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[GameControllerIssue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27765859/GameControllerIssue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"h